Substantive modifications by the Origin fork
--------------------------------------------

The following are the principal modifications made on top of upstream
Multica v0.2.21:

1.  Single-user local product reframing
    - Repositioned as a single-user local Agent workbench ("Origin"),
      with Mission as the primary user object and a hardcoded local
      workspace named `Fairy`.
    - Removed multi-tenant SaaS concepts from the product surface
      (workspace creation, member invitation, role management, cloud
      onboarding flows) — see §2.1 of docs/origin-product-architecture-prd.md
      (kept private to the fork) for the design rationale.
    - Replaced the email-and-verification-code login flow with a
      `/auth/local-signin` endpoint that takes only a name and avatar.

2.  New product objects (Origin Phase 1)
    - Idea Pool — lightweight pre-Mission incubation layer (migration 074).
    - Council Session — on-demand multi-agent rooms with activity-level
      gating (migration 075).
    - User Profile — per-(workspace,user) identity card and preferences
      block intended as the closest layer of a three-layer system prompt
      injection (migration 076).

3.  Frontend reductions
    - Removed `apps/web/` (the upstream Next.js web frontend) entirely.
      The Electron desktop app is the only first-class shell.
    - Removed `Dockerfile.web` and the `frontend` service from
      `docker-compose.selfhost*.yml`.
    - Removed several settings tabs that conflict with the single-user
      reframing (workspace info / repos / members / labs) and the
      auto-updater (which would overwrite the fork with stock Multica
      releases).

4.  UI polish
    - Origin avatar set (50 PNG presets) bundled as a deterministic
      offline avatar pool, replacing emoji and DiceBear remote URLs.
    - Sidebar header simplified from a workspace dropdown into a
      pure user-identity block; the avatar dropdown menu (which
      mixed account, workspace and logout actions) was removed.
    - Agent card density reduced; agents grid switched to
      `auto-fill / minmax(220px, 1fr)` for window-resize friendliness.
    - Help launcher rewritten to point at the upstream repository
      and license rather than the upstream documentation site.

The original Multica README (preserved verbatim from upstream) is available
